<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.5 percent in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.5 percent in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK bank notes in circulation rose 5.5 percent in the week to July 23 over the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said. Last week the rise was 5.6 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			 Latest week  Previous wk  year-ago wk</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.93    21.79	    20.79</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 2.60     2.65	     1.80</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
